   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Typical application circuit",
   "page": 1,
   "description": "Eighteen single LEDs, each with its anode on the battery rail and its cathode on one OUTn pin, so every channel sinks its own LED current. VCC also runs from the battery, decoupled by 1 µF and 0.1 µF. A microcontroller drives SDA and SCL, each pulled up to the logic rail VDD by 4.7 kΩ, and drives SDB, which a 100 kΩ resistor holds low (chip off) until the controller raises it. The 3.3 kΩ resistor from R_EXT to ground sets the full-scale channel current to about 23 mA.",
